        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Morocco and PSG player Hakimi to stand trial in Frace on rape charge France Issued on: 19/06/2026 - 16:46 Achraf Hakimi will stand trial for rape a Paris appeals court has ruled. The captain of the Moroccan team was first accused of rape in 2023, by a then 24 year old woman. In February this year, an investigative judge ruled that Hakimi would face trial followed recommendations from public prosecutors. The PSG right back appealed the decision, but today that appeal was quashed paving the way for Hakimi to be tried in a criminal court. Moroccan star footballer Hakimi to stand trial on rape charge 19/06/2026 Sport World Cup? Not today: New York is celebrating the Knicks 19/06/2026 Sport Israeli stands shut down for displaying offensive weaponry at French arms fair 18/06/2026 France French school forced to adapt to early heatwave driven by climate change 18/06/2026 France Is football coming home? English fans tell FRANCE 24 18/06/2026 Europe France examines bill to rein in ultra-fast-fashion's expansion 17/06/2026 France What is France hoping for by inviting Trump to have dinner in Versailles? 17/06/2026 Europe Messi becomes joint World Cup all-time scorer with hat trick against Algeria 17/06/2026 Sport Iconic Paris canal opens to swimmers as residents seek ways to cope with heatwave 17/06/2026 France"
