        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel and Hezbollah say they agree to truce despite renewed attacks Middle East Issued on: 19/06/2026 - 16:43 Israel and Hezbollah agreed a ceasefire on June 19 after deadly exchanges between the two sides in Lebanon put the deal to end the Middle East war under strain. At least 20 people were killed in Lebanon in fresh strikes, as well four Israeli soldiers. In response, the far-right Israeli National Security Minister Itamar Ben Gvir said \"all of Lebanon must burn\". FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky tells us more. Uncertainty remains amid postponed US-Iran talks and continued fighting in Lebanon 19/06/2026 Middle East Israeli military strikes southern Lebanon as US-Iran talks are postponed 19/06/2026 Middle East Israel steps up attacks in Lebanon amid fallout with US over Iran deal 19/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran peace negotiations abruptly called off amid growing criticism 19/06/2026 Middle East Iran says Trump agreed to deal terms 'out of desperation' as US Democrats blast agreement 19/06/2026 Americas Replay: US VP JD Vance defends Iran-US agreement and FRANCE 24's analysis 18/06/2026 Middle East For Israel, US-Iran deal a 'disaster' incompatible with its security interests 18/06/2026 Middle East As a result of Iran war, Gulf states 'diversifying defensively' 18/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran agreement leaves Israelis 'in profound state of shock' 18/06/2026 Middle East"
